[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 build for the [B]LG Optimus Pro C660 / C660h[/B] (muscat, Qualcomm MSM7227T, ARMv6, 240x320). It is built with the Omni 4.4 tree and runs on a trimmed 2.6.35 kernel, because the recovery partition of this phone is only [B]5 MB[/B] (MTD, 0x500000 bytes).

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only flash this on the LG C660 / C660h. The recovery partition is mtd2; writing this image anywhere else can brick the phone.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status[/B][/SIZE]

Build: [B]twrp-3.1.1-0.1-c660.img[/B] (4349952 bytes, fits in the 5242880-byte partition with about 0.9 MB to spare)
MD5: [B]311221fd214daf78530c269837f8a4a5[/B]

Tested on real hardware (LG-C660h):

[LIST]
[*]Boots to recovery, touchscreen works (240x320 watch theme)
[*]ADB in recovery
[*]The screen wakes up correctly after the screen timeout
[*]Reboot to system (it does not fall back into recovery)
[*]Installing a ZIP with [B]adb sideload[/B]
[*]USB mass storage of the microSD, including unmounting it from the phone
[*]Flashing the image with flash_image and reading it back (identical)
[*]Wipe data, cache and Dalvik cache, and installing a ZIP from the microSD with a script (OpenRecoveryScript)
[*]Backup and restore of /system, /data and /boot: a file placed in /data came back after wiping /data and restoring, and the phone booted normally
[*]Three recovery / system reboot cycles in a row without falling back into recovery or hanging
[*][B]Not tested by me:[/B] backing up /cache, the encrypted-backup options and restoring on a different unit
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Partition layout used[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]/boot, /recovery, /misc: MTD
[*]/system, /data, /cache: YAFFS2 on MTD
[*]/sdcard: microSD, vfat (mmcblk0p1). The C660 has no internal storage and there is no /sd-ext
[*]Backups go to /sdcard/TWRP/BACKUPS/0000000000000000/. The phone does not report a serial number (the kernel shows all zeros), so every C660 uses that folder name; keep backups of different phones apart yourself
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[B]Before starting:[/B] back up your current recovery and copy the backup away from the phone. You need root and ADB on the running system (CM7, or a rooted stock).

[CODE]adb shell dump_image recovery /sdcard/recovery_backup.img
adb pull /sdcard/recovery_backup.img
adb push twrp-3.1.1-0.1-c660.img /data/local/tmp/r.img
adb shell md5sum /data/local/tmp/r.img
adb shell flash_image recovery /data/local/tmp/r.img
adb shell dump_image recovery /data/local/tmp/rb.img
adb reboot recovery[/CODE]

The md5sum must match the one above before you write the partition. The read-back file (rb.img) is the whole 5 MB partition; its first 4349952 bytes must be identical to the image.

To go back, write your backup to the same partition with flash_image.

[SIZE="4"][B]Entering recovery[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]From Android: [CODE]adb reboot recovery[/CODE]
[*]With the phone off: hold [B]Volume Down + Home + Power[/B]
[/LIST]

