[SIZE="4"][B]Known limitations[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]No MTP.[/B] The recovery kernel is trimmed to fit the partition and the 2.6.35 gadget is the legacy LG one. Use USB mass storage (Mount menu), adb push or adb sideload instead.
[*][B]No internal storage.[/B] Everything you flash or back up goes to the microSD.
[*]The recovery has a small /sbin/sh (mksh) instead of busybox, so shell commands over adb are limited.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]What is different from other attempts[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]The KitKat adbd does not work on this kernel (legacy /dev/android_adb, no FunctionFS), so the recovery ships the Gingerbread adbd. That adbd also needs CONFIG_INET=y in the kernel, otherwise it exits and no adb interface appears at all.
[*]LG's bootloader leaves a flag in the misc partition and TWRP cannot write the boot control block on MTD, so "Reboot to system" used to end in recovery again. A small init service erases misc at boot.
[*]The command-mode LCD only refreshes on FBIOPAN_DISPLAY, so the screen showed a stale frame after the timeout. TW_FBIOPAN fixes it.
[*]adb sideload needs FUSE, which is enabled in the recovery kernel.
[/LIST]

